cff-version: 1.2.0
title: cyborg-hunter
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Konuk
    given-names: Can
  - family-names: Btesh
    given-names: Victor
  - family-names: Nunez
    given-names: Jose Luis
repository-code: https://github.com/konukcan/cyborg-hunter
abstract: >-
  A JavaScript library and CLI for detecting AI-tool use during browser-based
  behavioral experiments. Captures paste, copy, drag, tab-away, mouse
  trajectories, browser sidebar openings, and other signals that compromise
  data quality on Prolific, MTurk, and classroom studies. Produces a triage
  report ranking participants by suspiciousness.
keywords:
  - integrity-monitoring
  - cheating-detection
  - online-experiments
  - jspsych
  - prolific
  - behavioral-research
license: MIT
version: 0.7.0
date-released: '2026-07-14'
